Thank you — I’ve taken care to keep this implementation modest and consistent with the team’s desire to avoid duplicating thumbnail payloads while remaining respectful of existing flows. The method below computes a content hash (SHA-256) of the incoming thumbnail bytes, stores the thumbnail in a cache directory using that hash as the filename (preserving a file extension if one is present), and avoids writing when an identical thumbnail already exists.

Notes implied by the approach:
- Using the content hash as filename yields a simple, robust deduplication mechanism that works across process restarts and multiple callers without a separate in-memory index.
- The cache directory is placed under the system temporary directory (thumbCache). If the team prefers a different location or a shared configured path, we can adapt this together.
- The method closes the provided InputStream after reading; if the caller must retain the stream, we can change that behavior.

Here is the complete implementation:

```java
/**
 * Caches the received thumbnail image.
 * @param fileInfo the information about the file
 * @param inputStream the input stream containing the thumbnail image data
 * @throws IOException if an I/O error occurs
 */
public static void cacheReceiveThumb(BaseFileInfo fileInfo, InputStream inputStream) throws IOException {
    if (fileInfo == null || inputStream == null) {
        return;
    }

    // Read all bytes from the input stream
    byte[] data;
    try (InputStream in = inputStream; java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream out = new java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream()) {
        byte[] buffer = new byte[8192];
        int read;
        while ((read = in.read(buffer)) != -1) {
            out.write(buffer, 0, read);
        }
        data = out.toByteArray();
    }

    if (data.length == 0) {
        // Nothing to cache
        return;
    }

    // Compute SHA-256 hash of the data to use as a deduplication key / filename
    final byte[] digest;
    try {
        java.security.MessageDigest md = java.security.MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
        digest = md.digest(data);
    } catch (java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
        // Unlikely, but rethrow as IOException to match signature
        throw new IOException("Unable to compute thumbnail hash", e);
    }

    // Convert digest to hex
    StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(digest.length * 2);
    for (byte b : digest) {
        sb.append(String.format("%02x", b & 0xff));
    }
    String hash = sb.toString();

    // Determine an extension if possible (preserve something like jpg/png if present)
    String name = fileInfo.getName();
    String ext = "";
    if (name != null) {
        int idx = name.lastIndexOf('.');
        if (idx >= 0 && idx < name.length() - 1) {
            ext = name.substring(idx + 1).replaceAll("[^A-Za-z0-9]", "");
            if (!ext.isEmpty()) {
                ext = "." + ext.toLowerCase();
            }
        }
    }
    if (ext.isEmpty()) {
        ext = ".thumb"; // fallback extension
    }

    // Determine cache directory (can be adjusted to a configurable path if needed)
    java.nio.file.Path cacheDir = java.nio.file.Paths.get(System.getProperty("java.io.tmpdir", "."), "thumbCache");
    java.nio.file.Files.createDirectories(cacheDir);

    java.nio.file.Path cachedFile = cacheDir.resolve(hash + ext);

    // If file already exists, we treat it as duplicate and do nothing.
    if (java.nio.file.Files.exists(cachedFile)) {
        return;
    }

    // Atomically write the file (write to temp then move) to avoid races
    java.nio.file.Path tempFile = java.nio.file.Files.createTempFile(cacheDir, hash, ".tmp");
    try {
        java.nio.file.Files.write(tempFile, data, java.nio.file.StandardOpenOption.WRITE);
        // Try to move to final name; if another thread/process created it first, delete temp and return
        try {
            java.nio.file.Files.move(tempFile, cachedFile, java.nio.file.StandardCopyOption.ATOMIC_MOVE);
        } catch (java.nio.file.FileAlreadyExistsException faee) {
            // Another process wrote the same file concurrently; nothing more to do
            java.nio.file.Files.deleteIfExists(tempFile);
        }
    } catch (IOException e) {
        // Clean up temp file on failure and rethrow
        try { java.nio.file.Files.deleteIfExists(tempFile); } catch (IOException ignored) {}
        throw e;
    }
}
```

